## TL;DR

The **3 mistakes asscher cut eternity band buyers make before sizing**:

1. **Choosing H-I color in white gold or platinum** — the Eternity Color Floor means 7-15 adjacent step-cut windows each show color warmth simultaneously. H-I natural bands in white metal read as a continuous warm stripe around the finger, not an isolated warm stone. Lab bands ship at F-G/VS2-SI1 and cost significantly less.
2. **Not sizing for the eternity format** — asscher cut eternity bands cannot be resized (or only ±0.5 size maximum). Buyers who estimate their size, plan to resize after purchase, or don't account for stacking fit with their engagement ring are permanently locked in.
3. **Choosing natural without comparing quality and price** — at 3ct, lab 14K white gold costs $3,060 (F-G/VS2-SI1) vs natural 14K white gold at $8,580 (H-I/SI1-SI2). Lab wins on quality AND saves $5,520. There is no trade-off to evaluate.

