## Expert Summary

An asscher cut eternity band is one of the most architecturally distinctive wedding rings available — no other diamond shape creates the Hall of Corridors effect, the continuous geometric depth that runs across the band when multiple adjacent step-cut windows reflect each other. Round brilliant eternity bands create sparkle; asscher eternity bands create depth.

The three mistakes in the TL;DR are real, and they compound. A buyer who chooses H-I color in a white gold full eternity and sizes to their individual ring size without accounting for stacking ends up with a band that shows color warmth across every stone and doesn't fit comfortably with their engagement ring. These are not minor details — they are the core decisions that determine whether the band delivers the geometric corridor effect the buyer imagined.

Lab asscher eternity bands solve the color problem automatically at a lower price — the full eternity lab band starts at $2,676 for 2ct in F-G/VS2-SI1, while natural eternity at the same carat weight in lower quality costs $6,420. The Eternity Color Floor, the Hall of Corridors, and the quality comparison all point to the same conclusion.

> **Farzana's take:** The asscher eternity band is the most demanding thing I help buyers choose — not because it is complicated, but because there are three decisions that matter and most buyers only ask about one of them: carat weight. They do not ask about color grade across all the stones, and they do not ask about sizing for a stack. When all three are right — F-G color, exact size for the stack, lab quality — the asscher eternity band is the most impressive wedding ring in the category; when one is wrong, the buyer knows it on the first day they wear it.

